# Rust build output
/target/
/dist/
# side target dirs used by review/CI agents (cargo --target-dir into the repo) — pure build cache
/.review-target/

# Bundled-CPython cache: build.rs downloads + verifies the python-build-standalone tarball(s) here
# (one per build target, ~46 MB each) so incremental/offline builds skip the network. Generated,
# never source — must not be committed.
/vendor/

# Binary blobs generally don't belong in source. This covers the raw Chroma capture
# dumps under docs/chroma-shm-capture/, which are research scratch and stay out.
*.bin
/docs/chroma-shm-capture/

# EXCEPT the chroma_shm codec's assets, which are SOURCE, not scratch. chroma_shm.rs
# does include_bytes! on keystream.bin, so without it in git a fresh clone cannot
# compile neuron-host AT ALL — and since neuron-app depends on it, that means the whole
# project. The overwatch-*.bin fixtures are the same story for `cargo test`. This blanket
# rule used to swallow all six, and CI caught it on its first ever run: nobody had built
# this repo from a clean clone. ~152 KB total, fixed contents, no churn.
!/crates/neuron-host/src/adapters/chroma_shm_data/*.bin

# Runtime diagnostics and crash artifacts
# Transient build/test console captures (agents and humans redirecting cargo output while
# debugging: build_err.txt, test_out.txt, ...). Machine-specific paths, often mid-failure
# snapshots — never source, never evidence. Anchored to the repo root so a crate could still
# ship a legitimately-named file if one ever needs to exist.
/build_err.txt
/build_out*.txt
/err.txt
/test_err*.txt
/test_out*.txt
*.dmp
*.mdmp
# msys/Cygwin tool crash dumps (a crashing bash.exe drops bash.exe.stackdump in the cwd —
# machine-specific module addresses, never source)
*.stackdump
neuron-crash.log
/diagnostics/

# Side build lanes used by parallel review/hardening agents (cargo with CARGO_TARGET_DIR
# pointed into the repo) — pure build cache, same class as /target/. Anchored to the repo
# ROOT (not repo-wide) and matches any root dir containing `target-lane`, which also catches a
# bash-mangled CARGO_TARGET_DIR that strips path separators into one root dir name
# (e.g. `UsersMicha...target-lane-runroot/`), seen 2026-07-10.
/*target-lane*/

# Local/generated runtime state
/runtime/host/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Scratch screenshots and generated visual probes
/_*.png
/runtime/_*.png

# Local project notes and scratch files. Useful while building Neuron, but not
# part of the public repository.
/.local/
# Licence drafts and correspondence kept beside the repo for convenience. Empty in a
# clone; ignored so a future `git add -A` can never publish one by accident.
/legal/
# Agent harness state (worktrees, task locks). Machine-local, never source.
/.claude/
# Internal UX pentest write-up — working notes, not published docs.
/docs/UX-PENTEST.md

# Local editor/OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs + scratch probes (session diagnostics)
*.log
/_*.log

# Session scratch dirs (audio auditions, screenshots)
/_audio/
/_shots/

# Stray redirect artifact
/null

# Per-user RUNTIME + PERSONAL state — generated by the app, never source. May hold personal
# binds / recorded macros / device exports, so it stays out of version control entirely.
# NOT ignored: runtime/host/*.py — the Macro Host sidecar + the `neuron` prelude are first-party
# SOURCE that pyruntime.rs `include_str!`s into the binary, so a fresh clone must have them to
# compile. Git cannot un-ignore a file inside an ignored DIRECTORY, hence the /runtime/* form.
/runtime/*
!/runtime/host/
/runtime/host/*
!/runtime/host/neuron.py
!/runtime/host/neuron_host.py
/backups/
/macros/
# the app's RUNTIME macro store (seeded default copies + the `.defaults_seeded` marker) — generated on
# first launch; the SOURCE defaults live in neuron-core/src/macros/defaults/. Committing the marker
# would suppress seeding on every fresh checkout, so keep this dir out of version control.
crates/neuron-app/macros/
# compiled-macro cache from the RETIRED rust-dll engine (replaced by the Macro Host) — dead artifacts
crates/neuron-core/macros/cache/
/reference/
profiles/
__neuron_test_*.toml

# Live user config — the app writes these from defaults; personal binds don't belong in source.
# (covers both the repo root and the per-crate dev copies)
cast.toml
apps.toml
bindings.toml
feel.toml
gestures.json
app.toml
